{"records":[{"id":"y8dndzn3mg","title":"Genome-scale CRISPR screen identifies TMEM41B as a critical host factor required for coronavirus replication","description":"These data are part of the Supplemental Items associated with the manuscript entitled \"Genome-scale CRISPR screen identifies TMEM41B as a critical host factor required for coronavirus replication\". These files include Supplementary Data file 1-4.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-03-16T10:34:13.579Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/y8dndzn3mg","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/y8dndzn3mg"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Limeng","last_name":"Sun","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Virus","Screening","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"zhpg8xshp9","title":"Lawrence et al., PNAS 2026","description":"Data from “Lawrence et al., 2026 A Genome-Wide Screen Identifies that PLCG2 Restrains Lysosomal GCase Activity.\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-06-22T18:23:16.389Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/zhpg8xshp9","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/zhpg8xshp9"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Baris","last_name":"Bingol","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Natural Sciences"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"7jgbckpdr4","title":"CHARGE QRS Exome Chip study summary statistics ","description":"Summary statistics and readme file of the CHARGE QRS Exome study, titled \"Exome-chip meta-analysis identifies novel loci, including ADAMTS6 associated with cardiac conduction\". Genome Biology 2018. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2018-05-02T10:40:25.562Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/7jgbckpdr4","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/7jgbckpdr4"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Bram","last_name":"Prins","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Statistical Genetics","Summary Statistic"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"9x47wzy8x7","title":"A study of \"Genome-wide CRISPR screens reveal host factors critical for SARS-CoV-2 infection\" by Wei et al. Cell 2020","description":"Identification of host genes essential for SARS-CoV-2 infection may reveal novel therapeutic targets and inform our understanding of COVID-19 pathogenesis. Here, we performed genome-wide CRISPR screens in Vero-E6 cells with SARS-CoV-2, MERS-CoV, bat coronavirus HKU5 expressing the SARS-CoV-1 spike, and VSV expressing the SARS-CoV-2 spike. Together this identifies potential therapeutic targets for SARS-CoV-2 and reveals SARS-lineage specific and pan-coronavirus host factors that regulate susceptibility to highly pathogenic coronaviruses.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-10-15T21:29:14.06Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/9x47wzy8x7","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/9x47wzy8x7"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Craig","last_name":"Wilen","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["CRISPR","Middle East Respiratory Syndrome-Related Coronavirus","Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus 2","COVID-19"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"vg3r5355bj","title":"Code used for \"  An evolutionary model identifies the main selective pressures for the evolution of genome-replication profiles.\" ","description":"Code used for \"  An evolutionary model identifies the main selective pressures for the evolution of genome-replication profiles.\"\n\nAt each cell cycle, a yeast cell replicates its genome by a prescribed but stochastic temporal program encoded by the localization and strength of a set of discrete \"replication origins\" along the genome. This temporal program is of primary importance for cell viability and, consequently, on evolutionary time scale it is subject to selective pressures. By mathematical modelling of replication-origins evolution this study identifies the two main selective pressures responsible for evolutionary appearance and disappearance of replication origins.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-10-13T21:38:07.95Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/vg3r5355bj","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/vg3r5355bj"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"rossana","last_name":"droghetti","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Computer Simulation"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"hjmvnf48gh","title":"Liu et al., Epigenetic reprogramming shapes the cellular landscape of schwannoma: CyTOF data","description":"Cytof .fcs data for Liu et al., Epigenetic reprogramming shapes the cellular landscape of schwannoma, Nature Communications 2023","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-05-02T07:15:34.374Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/hjmvnf48gh","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/hjmvnf48gh"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Nam Woo","last_name":"Cho","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cancer Immunology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"zcf22sjps8","title":"Distinct Chromatin Scanning Modes Lead to Targeting of Compacted Chromatin by Pioneer Factors FOXA1 and SOX2","description":"Pioneer transcription factors interact with nucleosomes to scan silent, compact chromatin, enabling cooperative events that modulate gene activity.  While at a subset of sites, pioneer factors access chromatin by assisted loading with other transcription factors, the nucleosome binding properties of pioneer factors enable them to initiate zygotic genome activation, embryonic development, and cellular reprogramming.  To better understand nucleosome targeting in vivo, we assessed whether pioneer factors FoxA1 and Sox2 target stable or unstable nucleosomes and found that they target DNase-resistant, stable nucleosomes, whereas HNF4A, a non-nucleosome binding factor, targets open, DNase-sensitive chromatin.  Despite FOXA1 and SOX2 targeting similar proportions of DNase-resistant chromatin, using single-molecule tracking, we found that FOXA1 uses lower nucleoplasmic diffusion and longer residence times while SOX2 uses higher nucleoplasmic diffusion and shorter residence times to scan compact chromatin, while HNF4 does not scan compact chromatin.  Thus pioneer factors target compact chromatin through distinct processes.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-06-23T05:35:23.568Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/zcf22sjps8","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/zcf22sjps8"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jonathan","last_name":"Lerner","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Molecular Biology","Chromatin","Single Molecule Imaging"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"wkttx6tp2d","title":"S. aureus transposon sequencing in the murine vaginal tract ","description":"Results from TRANSIT Tn-seq conditional essentiality analysis, associated to the paper \"Genome-wide mutagenesis identifies factors involved in MRSA vaginal colonization \" by Lyon et al. (2025), under review at Cell Reports. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-02-18T22:39:47.454Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/wkttx6tp2d","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/wkttx6tp2d"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Laurie","last_name":"Lyon","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Transposon","Vagina","Mouse Model","Methicillin-Resistant Staphylococcus aureus"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"ktwhf64cxz","title":"Genome-wide association study identifies two novel susceptibility loci for trichilemmal cysts","description":"Trichilemmal cysts (TC), also known as pilar cysts, are keratin-filled, subepidermal nodules originating from the outer hair root sheath. Recently phospholipase C delta 1 has been suggested to play a critical role in the formation of TCs. However, it is unknown if other genes contribute to TC formation. We conducted a genome-wide association study (GWAS) of 5,331 TC cases and 403,251 controls in a genetically British group. Our genome-wide scan revealed PLCD1, CLPTM1L, and TMED10|FOS as susceptibility loci for TCs. Additionally, we performed a follow-up GWAS on 2,806 epidermal inclusion cysts and 405,776 controls in the same population, without identifying any susceptibility loci.  ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-05-20T08:07:22.23Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ktwhf64cxz","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/ktwhf64cxz"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Ahmed","last_name":"Yousaf","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Michael","last_name":"Kolodney","orcid":"0000-0003-1931-8644"}],"funders":[],"categories":["Dermatology","Genome Wide Association Study","Cyst"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"pnbjdtdkfg","title":"A genome-scale gain-of-function CRISPR screen in CD8 T cells identifies proline metabolism as a means to enhance CAR-T therapy ","description":"CyTOF raw data.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-02-14T13:21:30.568Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/pnbjdtdkfg","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/pnbjdtdkfg"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Lupeng","last_name":"Ye","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jonathan","last_name":"Park","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Sidi","last_name":"Chen","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Immunology"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":102607,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":108,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":102607,"collectio